  "overview": {
    "short": "Red Fort (Lal Qila) in Old Delhi is a 17th-century UNESCO World Heritage Mughal fortress constructed by Emperor Shah Jahan from red sandstone.",
    "description": "Rising majestically above Netaji Subhash Marg in Old Delhi, the Red Fort (Lal Qila) was commissioned by Mughal Emperor Shah Jahan in 1638 when he shifted his capital from Agra to Shahjahanabad. Enclosed within massive 33-metre-high red sandstone octagonal battlements, the complex houses imperial marvels including the Lahori Gate, Chhatta Chowk, Diwan-i-Aam, Diwan-i-Khas, Moti Masjid, and the lush Hayat Bakhsh Bagh gardens.",
